# The altioo-mcp release the weekly contract job installs in place of the stand-in
# (doc/ci-itop-matrix.md, "The real altioo-mcp, weekly"). Read by tools/ci/fetch-altioo-mcp.sh,
# which the workflow and tools/ci/local/run.sh both call, so the pin lives here and nowhere else.
#
# Bumped by hand, both lines together: the SHA-256 is the archive's, copied from the release's
# own altioo-mcp-<version>.zip.sha256 after reading it, and the fetch also checks the GitHub
# attestation in CI. A new altioo-mcp release is not picked up until someone moves this line,
# which is the point: a red weekly run then names the change that made it.
#
# @copyright   Copyright (C) 2026 Altioo
# @license     https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html AGPL-3.0-or-later
ALTIOO_MCP_VERSION=1.2.0
ALTIOO_MCP_SHA256=cdb860f01d9f8fa555aaac78adb7532944fb22e41fa94a712f944fefa0086fae
